---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const stages = [
  { n: '1', label: 'Bottle', detail: 'A clean, used PET drinking-water bottle.' },
  { n: '2', label: 'Filament', detail: 'Cut into a single continuous strand and re-formed at filament gauge on a Petamentor2 rebuild, ~185 °C, spool turning ~1 rpm.' },
  { n: '3', label: 'Part', detail: 'Printed from the shrinkage-compensated hardware/rpet/ geometry — not the standard STLs.' },
];
---
<section id="rpet">
  <div class="eyebrow">rPET</div>
  <h2>Bottles into filament — an optional, sustainable route.</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    rPET, recycled from used drinking-water bottles, is one of five
    materials the manifold was tested in, and the funnel and filter support
    can be printed in it directly.
  </p>

  <ol class="stages">
    {stages.map((s) => (
      <li>
        <span class="stage-n">{s.n}</span>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-label">{s.label}</div>
          <p class="stage-detail">{s.detail}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h3>Credit</h3>
  <p>
    The filament-making machine used is a rebuild of
    <strong>Petamentor2</strong>, an open-source PET-bottle-to-filament
    machine designed by <strong>Ondřej Šraitr</strong>:
    <a href="https://petamentor2.com/" rel="noopener">petamentor2.com</a>.
    The author of this project built a Petamentor2 himself — he did not
    design the machine. Its design files are Šraitr's work and are
    deliberately not redistributed in this repository; build your own from
    the upstream project.
  </p>

  <h3>Use the compensated geometry</h3>
  <p>
    rPET shrinks differently during cooling than ABS or PLA, so
    <code>hardware/rpet/</code> is dimensionally compensated for that
    shrinkage — printing the standard STLs in rPET will not fit. There is
    no separate rPET base: the base needs no compensation, so the same
    <code>hardware/stl/base.stl</code> is correct in every material,
    including rPET. rPET's print settings also differ enough from the ABS
    gas-tight profile that they don't carry over directly — see
    <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/docs/rpet.md`}>docs/rpet.md</a> for the
    settings source and the full bottle-to-filament procedure.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  #rpet h2 { max-width: 20ch; }
  #rpet h3 { font-size: 20px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }

  .stages {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 32px 0 40px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .stages li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 20px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .stage-n {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--accent-2);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stage-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .stage-detail {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  code {
    background: var(--bg-2);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: .92em;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
